\n- **R1-F4 (low): fixed.** The resource-limits draft spec now covers CPU affinity and I/O limits (R2, line 37) and measuring I/O (R4, line 38).\n\n## New findings (all low, follow-up)\n\nMost of these are places where the old memo-key description survived the F1 fix:\n\n- **N1** `.pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:298`: the ADR's Caches bullet still says the key is \"the commit, the shallow file and the repository config\".\n- **N2** `POSE.md:949`: the user documentation says the key is \"that commit and the shallow state\" and leaves out the Git config. The same text is in `locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944` and the copies under `pose-mcp/internal/scaffold/dist`.\n- **N3** `pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go:72`: the code comment says the repository config file is digested into the key, but the code only digests `shallow` now. The type comment at `:19` also leaves the config out.\n- **N4** `.pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md:20`: the draft spec's Goal (line 20) and Business value (line 24) still describe the config gap that has been fixed, while its R2 is withdrawn.\n- **N5** `.pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md:3`: the run that qualifies the milestone was measured before the key change. The fix adds one `git config` process per operation inside the runtime, so the T1/T6 figures describe the earlier code. This is likely negligible against a 25 s check, but it hasn't been measured.\n- **N6** `.pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md:37`: the roadmap still links the ADR as \"Proposed\".\n\n## Criteria\n\nAll seven pass:\n\n- **Integration:** the sealed integration runs for the CLI/MCP handoff, caches, runtime, resident cache and QoS all passed.\n- **Cut criteria and outcome:** each milestone's exit gate and the overall outcome are matched by delivered code and passing tests.\n- **End-to-end:** the opt-in runtime path (start/attach, run a check, stop), with standalone fallback, passes in the sealed runtime integration run.\n- **Milestones:** all six member specs and both engine specs are `done`. The milestones' own review records aren't in this checkout, as the implementer said.\n- **Release readiness:** there are six changelogs, the docs are in parity, and only low-severity doc drift remains.\n- **Residual risk:** each part of the roadmap's \"not delivered\" list has its own draft spec (`pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command`, `pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe`, `pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default`). No blocking risk remains.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"N1\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md\", \"line\": 298, \"summary\": \"The ADR's Caches bullet still says the resident memo key is 'the commit, the content of the shallow file and of the repository config'. The key now holds the digest of the effective Git configuration (every scope, includes followed), read once per operation.\", \"action\": \"Amend the Caches bullet of the 2026-11-10 amendment to describe the effective-configuration digest in the key\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N2\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"POSE.md\", \"line\": 949, \"summary\": \"The user documentation describes the resident memo key as 'that commit and the shallow state' and leaves out the effective Git configuration. The same text is in locales/pt-BR/POSE.md:944 and the scaffold dist copies.\", \"action\": \"Add the effective Git configuration to the key description in POSE.md, its pt-BR locale and the distributed copies\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/resident_git_memo.go\", \"line\": 72, \"summary\": \"The comment says the shallow file and the repository config have their content digested into the key, but only 'shallow' is read here now; the configuration arrives as the effective-config digest. The type comment at line 19 also says the key holds only the commit and the shallow state.\", \"action\": \"Update the comments at lines 19 and 72-73 to match the key\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N4\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md\", \"line\": 20, \"summary\": \"The draft spec's Goal (line 20) and Business value (line 24) still say the key lacks the global and user Git configuration, while its R2 is withdrawn because that was fixed. The draft's intent contradicts its requirements.\", \"action\": \"Rewrite the Goal and Business value (and maybe the title) to cover only memo_hits per operation and the budget-admission test\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N5\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/reports/2026-11-09-pose-worktree-runtime-measurements.md\", \"line\": 3, \"summary\": \"The measurement run that qualifies the milestone predates the key change, which adds one 'git config --list' process per root per operation inside the runtime. The T1 and T6 figures describe the earlier code. The cost is probably negligible but has not been measured.\", \"action\": \"Re-run TestMeasureTheRuntimeOnTheRealRepository on the current key, or record in the report that the run predates it\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"},\n    {\"id\": \"N6\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \".pose/roadmaps/pose-shared-runtime.md\", \"line\": 37, \"summary\": \"The roadmap links the ADR as 'Proposed', but the ADR status is now 'Accepted for the delivered scope'.\", \"action\": \"Update the link text in the roadmap's continuation section\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2027-02-08\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"governance_read_view_git.go:52-68 (effectiveGitConfig digests 'git config --list -z --includes' once per operation per root; empty when unreadable) and :363 (passed into residentGitKey); resident_git_memo.go:62-86 (key holds the config digest; empty config means not memoized). Tests: resident_git_memo_test.go:56-67 and :120-153 (a user-config edit changes the key in the next operation, not within the current one), sealed unit:pose-mcp/go/test pass. Draft spec pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key R2 withdrawn (line 37).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/runtime_host.go:134,145,152 still take memo_hits as the difference of the global ResidentGitMemoStats counter around the command. Remains a low follow-up tracked as R1 of draft spec .pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-memo-hits-and-git-config-key.md:36.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/adr/2026-10-14-shared-domain-and-optional-worktree-runtime.md:5-13: status now reads 'Accepted for the delivered scope — 2026-11-10' and lists delivered and not-adopted items, consistent with the 2026-11-10 amendment (lines 275-313).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F4\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \".pose/specs/2026-11-10-pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command.md:37 (R2: CPU affinity and io.max configurable and reported) and :38 (R4: measurement includes I/O).\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Pinned checkout 80b49143 (clean). Read the roadmap (all milestones, exit gates, Estado/Entrega paragraphs), the full ADR including the B31, B33 and B35 amendments, the measurement report, and the resident memo path (resident_git_memo.go, governance_read_view_git.go effectiveGitConfig/capture, governance_git_pure.go pure-read classifier, git_snapshot_integrity.go gitCommandContext) and its tests. Read runtime_host.go hosted run and lanes, and runtime_cmd.go admission flags and memo enablement. Checked status of the six member specs and two engine specs (all done) and the four draft follow-up specs (resource limits, named pipe, route by default, memo hits). Checked POSE.md, pt-BR and scaffold dist command reference and runtime prose for memo-key consistency; scripts/bench_governance.py coverage via the Go integration test (governance_operation_performance_test.go:384,538); validation-matrix coverage of the scripts component (none); and which milestone review records are present in this checkout. The profile denied go test and the pose plan tools, so test and tool results come from the sealed evidence.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Component boundaries are CLI to domain (common_operation), MCP to domain (route_inventory classes, typed handoff), runtime socket to CLI dispatch (runtime_host, worktreeruntime) and domain to Git memo. All are covered by passing sealed integration runs: common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff, cli-mcp-operation-results, bounded-isolated-graph-caches, optional-worktree-runtime, resident-cache and runtime-qos.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cut-criteria\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/runtime-qos-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined each exit gate against delivered code and sealed evidence. B32: governance-operation-performance-integration, isolated benchmark. B31: route classes and typed handoff, common-domain integration. B33: byte budgets per owner and global, single-flight, deep copy and view, bounded-isolated-graph-caches-integration. B35: identity/handshake, 0600 socket with peer credentials, lifecycle, standalone and Windows fallback, lanes with deterministic output (T5) and per-scenario RAM/CPU/latency (T1-T7 in the measurement report), optional-worktree-runtime/resident-cache/runtime-qos integrations. The departures (no CPU quota or affinity, no per-command limits, Windows standalone) are declared in the roadmap and ADR and drafted as specs. With F1 fixed, the no-stale-cache and deterministic-output gates hold.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"end-to-end\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The user path is opt-in: 'pose runtime start/attach/status/run/stop', and 'pose runtime run' falls back to standalone when no compatible runtime exists. It is exercised end to end by the sealed optional-worktree-runtime, resident-cache and runtime-qos integrations. The measurement report records hosted output byte-identical to standalone (T5) and fallback overhead (T6). The commands are documented at POSE.md:260-261.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestones\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-operation-performance-integration\", \"rationale\": \"All four milestones' member specs are status done (operation-performance 2026-11-03, common-domain 2026-11-09, bounded caches 2026-11-08, the three runtime slices 2026-11-09/10), plus the two engine specs. The roadmap states each milestone closed with independent review. This checkout does not hold the milestone review records (the implementer disclosed this), so per the brief I judged the roadmap state and each milestone's integration evidence, all of which pass.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"outcome\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/resident-cache-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Outcome: coherent CLI/MCP operations (common domain, route classes, typed handoff), controlled cost per producer (B32 measurement), bounded reuse (B33 byte-budgeted caches; resident memo with byte budget and LRU) and an optional runtime adopted only after identity, coherence, authorization and recovery were qualified (handshake refuses mismatches; no authority conferred; ambiguous runs not retried; restart inherits nothing, T2). Warm review-check takes 0.41 of cold time with identical output. The F1 fix closes the coherence gap of round 1.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"release-readiness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"There are unreleased changelogs for all six member specs, the POSE.md command reference and its pt-BR and scaffold dist copies are in parity (sealed parity integration), and no migration is required because the runtime is opt-in. Remaining drift in the memo-key wording (N1, N2, N4, N6) and a measurement taken before the key change (N5) are low-severity follow-ups.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"residual-risk\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"No blocking risk remains: R1-F1, the only medium, is fixed. R1-F2 and N1-N6 are low follow-ups with action, owner and review_by. Each part of the roadmap's not-delivered list has its own draft spec (pose-runtime-resource-limits-per-command now including affinity and I/O, pose-runtime-windows-named-pipe, pose-checks-route-to-the-runtime-by-default).\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool. The review profile denied shell execution of pose commands in this run, so the change was swept by reading the code instead.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool. The review profile denied shell execution in this run. scripts/bench_governance.py and bench-governance.sh were read and are exercised through governance_operation_performance_test.go.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/common-domain-and-cli-mcp-handoff-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Not run by the reviewer (the profile denies the shell). Disposed on the sealed integration evidence for the component boundaries this roadmap introduced, all passing.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool. The review profile denied shell execution. Debt observed by reading (stale key descriptions, the global memo_hits counter) is reported as findings.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Its precondition is the completion of this review; it cannot pass before the attestation is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"roadmap-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/optional-worktree-runtime-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Not run by the reviewer (the profile denies the shell). Disposed on the sealed integration evidence of the roadmap's milestones, all passing.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool. The review profile denied shell execution. The reviewer chose files to read from the change list directly.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool. The review profile denied shell execution. The two scripts in the change were read directly.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The sealed strict validation run of pose-mcp passed. Not re-run by the reviewer because the profile denies the shell.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"scripts\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"producer_coverage\": \"none\", \"rationale\": \"No registered check in .pose/indexes/validation-matrix.json covers the scripts component (producer_coverage none), so validate has no producer for it. The scripts are exercised indirectly by pose-mcp's governance-operation-performance integration test.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":1784,"type":"result","duration_ms":173501,"uuid":"f1ac6b6d-b606-4aba-aa09-df2f25aea52f","ttft_stream_ms":707,"time_to_request_ms":47,"first_content_frame_ms":707,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":44,"outputTokens":19202,"cacheReadInputTokens":1241798,"cacheCreationInputTokens":71148,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.2017596,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7278,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":71148,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-04T10:05:09.044Z"}
